1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,560
Hello, Sandy. How have you been getting on with your dissertation?

2
00:00:03,560 --> 00:00:08,630
Fine, and I've been working hard on the various action points we agreed on our last tutorial.

3
00:00:08,630 --> 00:00:10,800
Do you want to talk me through what you've done?

4
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:15,835
Yeah, sure. Well, we agreed on three main targets for me to aim for.

5
00:00:15,835 --> 00:00:20,150
The first one was to find out about suitable data analysis software.

6
00:00:20,150 --> 00:00:20,770
Yes.

7
00:00:20,770 --> 00:00:25,060
And what I decided to do was to look through catalogues specializing in IT.

8
00:00:25,060 --> 00:00:27,680
That's a good idea. What did you come up with?

9
00:00:27,680 --> 00:00:30,310
I found the names of two promising ones.

10
00:00:30,310 --> 00:00:30,770
Right.

11
00:00:30,770 --> 00:00:34,200
But I also thought it'd be worthwhile talking to a lecturer.

12
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:36,740
Oh right. Who did you see?

13
00:00:36,740 --> 00:00:41,100
Jane Prince. Do you know her? She's in the Computer Centre.

14
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:43,490
Yes, of course, she's the new Head.

15
00:00:43,490 --> 00:00:45,400
Yes. Well, she was very helpful.

16
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:48,800
Oh, that's good. Did she suggest anything in particular?

17
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:50,729
Yeah. She recommended software called Vivat

18
00:00:50,729 --> 00:00:55,230
and said I should book up for a couple of practice sessions using Vivat.

19
00:00:55,230 --> 00:00:57,340
Great. I'm sure you'll find them useful.

20
00:00:57,340 --> 00:01:02,580
And, of course, the second target was to draw up a survey checklist which I...

21
00:01:02,580 --> 00:01:05,140
Yes, you emailed me it last week.

22
00:01:05,140 --> 00:01:06,630
Have you had a chance to look...?

23
00:01:06,630 --> 00:01:09,510
Of course, um I think it's good.

24
00:01:09,510 --> 00:01:11,978
Very much on the right lines.

25
00:01:11,978 --> 00:01:15,680
I'd say your first two sections are spot on.

26
00:01:15,680 --> 00:01:18,971
I wouldn't suggest that you change anything there,

27
00:01:18,971 --> 00:01:24,730
but in section three you really do need to have questions on teaching experience.

28
00:01:24,730 --> 00:01:27,450
Yeah. I was thinking that section looked a bit short.

29
00:01:27,450 --> 00:01:28,000
Right.

30
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:33,030
And my third target was, do further reading on discipline.

31
00:01:33,030 --> 00:01:35,600
Oh yes. I mentioned a couple of writers, didn't I?

32
00:01:35,600 --> 00:01:39,545
Yes, well I got hold of the Banerjee and I thought that was excellent.

33
00:01:39,545 --> 00:01:44,054
But I'm afraid I didn't manage to get hold of the essays about classroom management. You know,

34
00:01:44,054 --> 00:01:45,463
the ones by Simon Ericsson.

35
00:01:45,463 --> 00:01:49,690
The bookshop said it was out of print and the library doesn't have a copy.

36
00:01:49,690 --> 00:01:53,893
Oh right, and I'm afraid I've lent my copy to another student.

37
00:01:53,893 --> 00:01:58,120
What I suggest you do is try the library again

38
00:01:58,280 --> 00:02:00,897
This time apply for it through the service called special loans.

39
00:02:00,897 --> 00:02:05,100
Have you done that before? You're entitled to six books a year.

40
00:02:05,100 --> 00:02:08,000
Yes. No problem. That's what I'll do.

41
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:10,250
So, lots of useful work done.

42
00:02:10,250 --> 00:02:13,140
So, let's look at some new targets.

43
00:02:13,140 --> 00:02:17,268
We'll start by having a chat about your Chapter One.

44
00:02:17,268 --> 00:02:19,745
I very much enjoyed reading it.

45
00:02:19,745 --> 00:02:22,222
Your written style is very clear

46
00:02:22,222 --> 00:02:27,589
and you've included lots of interesting descriptions of education in your target area.

47
00:02:27,589 --> 00:02:32,130
I've just got a couple of suggestions for some additional work.

48
00:02:32,130 --> 00:02:36,530
Of course. Could I just ask - what do you think I should call it?

49
00:02:36,530 --> 00:02:40,900
Well, I'd go for something like Context Review. What do you think?

50
00:02:40,900 --> 00:02:42,880
Well, short and to the point.

51
00:02:42,880 --> 00:02:46,009
Exactly. Now, as regards specific areas to work on,

52
00:02:46,009 --> 00:02:51,920
I'd be quite interested to have a few more statistics about the schools in the different zones.

53
00:02:51,920 --> 00:02:54,720
Oh, that wouldn't be a problem. I can get them from the Internet.

54
00:02:54,720 --> 00:02:59,257
Great, and although you did make a reference to quite a few different writers,

55
00:02:59,257 --> 00:03:03,470
I think you should aim to cite more works written later than 2000.

56
00:03:03,470 --> 00:03:09,060
OK. That's more difficult, but I can try. When do you want that done by?

57
00:03:09,060 --> 00:03:13,172
Oh, it's not urgent. Um I should aim for the end of term.

58
00:03:13,172 --> 00:03:17,600
But in the meantime, I think you should also be thinking about Chapter Two.

59
00:03:17,600 --> 00:03:19,630
Should I be drafting it already?

60
00:03:19,630 --> 00:03:22,530
No, but I think you should note down its main sections.

61
00:03:22,530 --> 00:03:26,140
Yes. You know, I always find that the hardest part.

62
00:03:26,140 --> 00:03:29,600
I always find it helpful to put some ideas on index cards.

63
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:30,200
Yeah.

64
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:32,560
Um... and then you can sort them

65
00:03:32,560 --> 00:03:35,400
and even lay them out on the floor. It's a real help.

66
00:03:35,400 --> 00:03:39,630
Well, I'll certainly try it! When would the deadline be for that?

67
00:03:39,630 --> 00:03:44,355
My advice would be to get it done before you embark upon the research.

68
00:03:44,355 --> 00:03:47,730
You can always change it later if you need to.

69
00:03:47,730 --> 00:03:49,370
OK. I'll get going on that then.
